rkets declining. Looking at the market, A-shares today staged a long-lost style of \"real estate ignition, consumer relay\" linkage trend, with many real estate leading stocks such as China Vanke Co., Ltd., Greenland Holdings Corporation seeing large gains. Analysis pointed out that the rise in real estate stocks was mainly due to two reasons: first, the issuance of the \"15th Five-Year Plan for Urban Renewal\" by the State Council last night; and second, the sector had experienced more than ten consecutive days of decline, creating room for a rebound. While real estate stocks were rising, the consumer sector also saw significant gains, with sectors like hotel catering and liquor leading the way, with Jiugui Liquor hitting the limit up. During the day, growth stocks that were previously hot, such as chips and computational power, experienced a dive in prices. In the short term, the possibility of a change in market style cannot be ruled out. In other hot spots, coal, electricity concepts continued to rise, with stocks like Jinneng Holding Shanxi Electric Power, Huadian Energy hitting the limit up; heavyweight sectors such as securities, banks, insurance, futures, and special evaluation collectively supported the market, with Nanhua Futures, Financial Street Holdings hitting the limit up; concepts like agriculture, breeding, whole vehicles, and unified large markets showed overall strength. On the downside, storage chips, the semiconductor industry chain suffered heavy losses, with stocks like Suzhou Delphi Laser falling by over 10%; satellite communication, satellite internet concepts continued to decline, with Chongqing Zaisheng Technology Corp. hitting the limit down; humanoid Siasun Robot\u0026Automation concept showed a downward trend, with computational hardware stocks experiencing a full-scale pullback. Huatai recently pointed out that the market has entered a period of adjustment after a high surge, with short-term internal and external risks interwoven, curr